# Editor tools — UI Toolkit first

When adding or rewriting **Editor** tools in **griddungeon-game**, use **UI Toolkit** (`CreateGUI`, `CustomEditor` + `CreateInspectorGUI`, UXML/USS under `Assets/UI/Editor/`, custom `VisualElement` panels) instead of new `OnGUI` / `EditorGUILayout`, unless UITK cannot meet the requirement (comment why).

Player-facing UITK rules still apply where relevant: **BEM** class names in UXML/USS (`unity-ui-toolkit.mdc`), **USS subset** limits (`unity-uitk-uss-limits.mdc`).

Examples: `FloorEditorWindow`, `GridDungeonSaveEditorWindow`, `EncounterGroupEditor`, `EnemySlotListInspector`.

## Custom UITK inspector for ScriptableObjects (pattern)

Use this when adding `[CustomEditor(typeof(YourScriptableObject))]` with `CreateInspectorGUI()` — not default IMGUI.

### Layout recipe

| Layer | Responsibility |
|-------|----------------|
| **Root `VisualElement`** | Block BEM class (e.g. `encounter-group-editor`), load feature USS + `Assets/UI/Editor/Shared/EditorFoldoutCard.uss` when using bordered foldout lists |
| **`EditorContentDatabaseField`** | Top row when inspector uses **content-id dropdowns** (enemies, story events, encounters, items, …) |
| **`PropertyField`** | Plain serialized fields with no catalog picker |
| **Custom `VisualElement` panels** | Repeated lists, foldout cards, catalog-backed pickers (`*ListInspector`, `*DefinitionField`) |
| **`root.Bind(serializedObject)`** | Once at end — binds all `PropertyField` descendants |

### C# skeleton

```csharp
[CustomEditor(typeof(MyContentAsset))]
public sealed class MyContentAssetEditor : UnityEditor.Editor
{
    const string k_StylePath = "Assets/UI/Editor/MyFeature/MyContentAssetInspector.uss";

    public override VisualElement CreateInspectorGUI()
    {
        var root = new VisualElement();
        root.AddToClassList("my-content-editor");

        StyleSheet? sheet = AssetDatabase.LoadAssetAtPath<StyleSheet>(k_StylePath);
        if (sheet != null)
        {
            root.styleSheets.Add(sheet);
        }

        var catalogPanel = new MyCatalogListInspector(serializedObject);

        // Catalog pickers: scope field first; refresh panels when database changes.
        root.Add(new EditorContentDatabaseField(catalogPanel.RefreshCatalogSources));

        root.Add(new PropertyField(serializedObject.FindProperty("m_plainField")));
        root.Add(catalogPanel);

        root.Bind(serializedObject);
        return root;
    }
}
```

### Content-id pickers (required when inspector lists ContentDatabase entries)

Do **not** bind content ids as raw string `PropertyField` when a registered catalog exists — use a `PopupField` / `ObjectField` backed by a catalog helper.

| Do | Don't |
|----|-------|
| `EnemyDefinitionCatalog.GetRegisteredEnemyIds()` (defaults to scope) | `new PropertyField(enemyIdProp)` for pick-from-roster ids |
| `EditorContentDatabaseScope.Resolve()` in catalog loaders | `LoadAssetAtPath<ContentDatabase>("Assets/Content/…")` per tool |
| `RefreshCatalogSources()` on list/picker panels; call from scope field callback | Stale dropdown after user picks a different database |
| Warning label when id missing from active database | Silent empty dropdown |

Catalog panels expose **`public void RefreshCatalogSources()`** that rebuilds pickers (see `EnemySlotListInspector`, `EncounterEventsInspector`).

### Foldout list rows

See **Foldout inside bordered cards** below — apply to SO list inspectors (events, slots, table rows).

### File layout

```
Assets/Scripts/Editor/Content/     — CustomEditor + *Inspector / *Field / *Catalog
Assets/UI/Editor/<Feature>/        — *.uss (BEM), optional *.uxml
```

Match block name to SO domain (`encounter-group-editor`, not generic `inspector`).

