## Foldout inside bordered cards (required)

Unity `Foldout` toggle uses **negative left margin** (default inspector alignment). If you wrap a `Foldout` in a bordered/padded parent `VisualElement`, the **collapse arrow renders outside the box**.

| Do not | Do instead |
|--------|------------|
| `card.Add(foldout)` where `card` owns border/padding/background | Apply card BEM classes **on the `Foldout` root** |
| Assume `margin-left: 0` on the foldout alone fixes toggle bleed | Reset **toggle and content** child margins in USS |
| `PropertyField` on **array/list** serialized props | Custom list inspector with **`editor-foldout-card`** foldout + per-row `PropertyField` for elements |

### C# pattern

```csharp
var foldout = new Foldout { text = header, value = open };
foldout.AddToClassList("editor-foldout-card");
foldout.Add(content);
return foldout; // not wrapped in a separate VisualElement card
```

### USS / UXML pattern

Use shared **`Assets/UI/Editor/Shared/EditorFoldoutCard.uss`** — load on the inspector/window root alongside feature USS.

```css
/* EditorFoldoutCard.uss — apply class on Foldout root */
.editor-foldout-card { … border/padding … margin-left: 0; }
.editor-foldout-card > .unity-foldout__toggle { margin-left: 0; }
.editor-foldout-card > .unity-foldout__content { margin-left: 0; }
```

```xml
<!-- UXML editor tools: import shared sheet; class on Foldout, not a wrapper -->
<Style src="../Shared/EditorFoldoutCard.uss" />
<ui:Foldout text="Row title" class="editor-foldout-card">
    <!-- fields -->
</ui:Foldout>
```

Do **not** duplicate border/toggle-reset rules in feature USS — extend shared sheet only when a feature needs overrides.

When both card and foldout modifiers apply to the same node (C#), one class `editor-foldout-card` on the `Foldout` is enough.

